<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eberhard I, Duke of Württemberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1445">1445</a>–<a href="/years/1496">1496</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Eberhard im Bart, Eberhard the Bearded</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eberhard I, Duke of Württemberg, called the Bearded (im Bart), was count of Württemberg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bad-urach">Urach</a> from 1459 as Eberhard V. He founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/university-of-tubingen">University of Tübingen</a> in 1477 and reunited the divided county by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-munsingen">Treaty of Münsingen</a> in 1482. Emperor Maximilian I raised Württemberg to a duchy at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diet-of-worms-1495">Diet of Worms</a> in 1495, making Eberhard its first duke.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eberhard-i-duke-of-wurttemberg.jpg" alt="Eberhard I, Duke of Württemberg" width="320" height="502" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nicolaus Ochsenbach · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:900-101_Eberhard_im_Bart.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
